{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1411362-advice-about-a-tarot-based-mage","id":1411362,"title":"Advice about a Tarot-based Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-01T09:47:39-07:00","id":1411362,"title":"Advice about a Tarot-based Mage","content":"Hi. <br /> <br /> I started a Mage chronicle this year, and I'm getting used to everything after more than a decade of not-playing Mage. <br /> <br /> One of my players is a newbie whose character is a Hermetic based around Tarot cards. She basically conjures effects using the allegories of the Major Arcana (which - under that interpretation - can call up pretty much any effect). Those have been her main foci (or instruments if you want to use M20 lexicon) so far. I havent pushed her to integrate more hermetic stuff (powders, crystals, magic words, etc) into her paradigm because, as I mentioned before, shes a newbie.<br /> <br /> Last session she didnt have the cards at hand and felt really frustrated because, even though she had ideas for using her magic, she couldnt due to the absence of her main instrument. I wanted to use the situation as a learning opportunity for her, to show her the disadvantages of being to tied to a single instrument (or sets of instruments). Thing is, when it comes to give her advice about other things she could integrate to her paradigm - without losing her predilection for the cards and without tossing random hermetic stuff just because - Im out of ideas. <br /> <br /> Any recommendation about practices, or other instruments she could combine with the cards in a thematically-fitting way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T10:11:08-07:00","id":1411366,"title":"","content":"She could get the various cards tattooed onto her body","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T10:16:13-07:00","id":1411368,"title":"","content":"Point out to her that there's more to the Tarot than the Major Arcana. Get her thinking about the Tarot's meanings for the different suits (cups, swords, coins, wands); and from there, get her thinking about using <i>actual</i> cups or other containers, swords or knives, coins or pentacles, and wands or staves as stand-ins for the cards. Once she's used to the idea of substituting physical props for Tarot cards, get her thinking about what kinds of substitutions could be made for various Major Arcana. <br /> <br /> The whole thing will still essentially be Tarot-based; but ideally it will end up being less Tarot <i>card</i> based and more <i>symbolism of the</i> Tarot based.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T10:18:40-07:00","id":1411369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1411362-advice-about-a-tarot-based-mage?p=1411368#post1411368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point out to her that there's more to the Tarot than the Major Arcana. Get her thinking about the Tarot's meanings for the different suits (cups, swords, coins, wands); and from there, get her thinking about using <i>actual</i> cups or other containers, swords or knives, coins or pentacles, and wands or staves as stand-ins for the cards. Once she's used to the idea of substituting physical props for Tarot cards, get her thinking about what kinds of substitutions could be made for various Major Arcana.<br /> <br /> The whole thing will still essentially be Tarot-based; but ideally it will end up being less Tarot <i>card</i> based and more <i>symbolism of the</i> Tarot based.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dataweaver, this is PURE GOLD. It is just what I needed. Thank you very, very much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T10:33:45-07:00","id":1411373,"title":"","content":"As someone who has actually studied the Tarot, I totally second what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> said. Good luck!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T10:41:06-07:00","id":1411379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1411362-advice-about-a-tarot-based-mage?p=1411373#post1411373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who has actually studied the Tarot, I totally second what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> said. Good luck!</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to read that from someone who has actual knowledge about the topic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In my case, one of the good things about Mage is that it definitely leads me to knowledge - superficial at least - one way or another. I have done a lot of research about a lot of stuff just because of that chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T11:23:37-07:00","id":1411391,"title":"","content":"Awesome \ud83d\ude0a. Sounds like a cool chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T11:26:27-07:00","id":1411393,"title":"","content":"The four Tarot suites are all corner stones of certain parts of Hermetic (and most Western) ritual magic. Pentacles, cups, coins and blades are all used in rituals and rites, and each has a lot of mystical significance and meaning behind them. They're also the basis behind modern playing cards (Swords = Spades, Coins = Diamonds, Cups = Hearts, Pentacles = Clubs). The simplest way to build off of the Tarot as far as foci/tools would be using some sort of blade (ceremonial dagger or sword, or the like), a ritual cup/chalice, one or more coins or gemstones of significance, and chalk or other implements for drawing pentacles. (Alternately, if you're into the sort of modernist Chaos magic influenced Hermeticism that House Thig was big on, you could swap those out for their modern equivalents like a gun and credit cards.) Language/chanting/writing is also a big Hermetic focus. Especially of you can learn the True Names of certain spirits or other entities tied to certain cards. <br /> <br /> The Awakened also have their own associations for parts of the Tarot. Back in the day, there was even a <i>Mage Tarot Deck</i> made, which the included booklet discussing the suites' associations with both the four Avatar Essences and the four factions of the Ascension War (Traditions, Technocracy, Marauders, Nephandi), and the Major Arcana's associations with various WoD elements. (It also had suggestions for using it as a method of character creation and as a ST tool in various ways.) You can get a reproduction of it from DriveThruRPG's <a href=\"https://www.drivethrucards.com/product/223145/Mage-The-Ascension-Tarot\" target=\"_blank\">DriveThruCards section</a>. <br /> (I've long wished I could get the Sons of Ether-as-The Chariot and the Euthantos-as-Wheel of Fortune images blown up to poster size.)<br /> <br /> And thou it was made for Mage: The Awakening, the <i>Keys to the Supernal Tarot</i> book has a lot of interesting ideas to mine. <br /> <br /> And if you've never read Alan Moore's Promethea, it delves into a lot of classic Western mysticism, including an entire issue devoted to explaining the Major Arcana of the Tarot as the magicians journey from the ignorance of the Fool to the enlightenment of The World/Universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T15:05:57-07:00","id":1411439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1411362-advice-about-a-tarot-based-mage?p=1411391#post1411391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome \ud83d\ude0a. Sounds like a cool chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is the best one I have run in years and Im really proud about how it is turning out. It has made me really happy in this sad pandemic world. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T15:10:59-07:00","id":1411440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1411362-advice-about-a-tarot-based-mage?p=1411393#post1411393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you've never read Alan Moore's Promethea, it delves into a lot of classic Western mysticism, including an entire issue devoted to explaining the Major Arcana of the Tarot as the magicians journey from the ignorance of the Fool to the enlightenment of The World/Universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im actually reading Promethea after I saw it recommended on this forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T17:01:05-07:00","id":1411593,"title":"","content":"It might be good to look at some of the popular Tarot card deck designs for imagery that could be incorporated directly into practice. Geometric designs, scales, and other tools tend to feature prominently in the decks I saw. She may be more comfortable incorporating those symbols. Also, perhaps she could take drawing/images and make her own tarot related imagery on the go. It wouldn't be as effective as a real deck, but could maybe work on the go. (i.e. making an image of the Sun or Tower on a brick wall with spray paint...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T18:08:13-07:00","id":1411597,"title":"","content":"There are dozens of Tarot deck designs she could mine for images. Also two new Major Arcana cards, Separation and the Farrier (blacksmith), and four Ladies one for each suit that somebody developed back in the Seventies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T07:45:43-07:00","id":1411799,"title":"","content":"Another option to get her more comfortable with expanding her practice may be to have her &quot;embody&quot; the persona on some of the cards. For example, perhaps you can introduce the idea that she has to BECOME the Magician, Hierophant or High Priestess in this scenario and have her approach from that angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T09:02:26-07:00","id":1411806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1411362-advice-about-a-tarot-based-mage?p=1411799#post1411799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another option to get her more comfortable with expanding her practice may be to have her &amp;quot;embody&amp;quot; the persona on some of the cards. For example, perhaps you can introduce the idea that she has to BECOME the Magician, Hierophant or High Priestess in this scenario and have her approach from that angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds good having Different personas for different tasks, one of my characters has a secret backup personality in case the main one is mentally compromised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T21:34:39-07:00","id":1412217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1411362-advice-about-a-tarot-based-mage?p=1411799#post1411799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another option to get her more comfortable with expanding her practice may be to have her &quot;embody&quot; the persona on some of the cards. For example, perhaps you can introduce the idea that she has to BECOME the Magician, Hierophant or High Priestess in this scenario and have her approach from that angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>The art of Theurgy was a thing in Ancient Greece, in which one would invoke the action/evoke the presence of a specific deity or higher power in order to disclose sacred mysteries, perfect oneself, and ultimately unite with the divine (effectively Ascension from a Mage point of view). This sort of thing continued through the Middle Ages and Renaissance, and was a part of 19th and 20th century ritual magic. While this frequently involved the idea of angels (especially those associated with various planetary bodies and the like), it could easily also include the idea of powerful Incarna or Celestines which are represented by/associated with the Major Arcana and evoking their power. (It could also be used to channel said spirits into inanimate objects, usually statues, which be a fairly cool way to use Spirit and Matter magic to bring objects to life for a short period.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T14:43:11-07:00","id":1412910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1411362-advice-about-a-tarot-based-mage?p=1411393#post1411393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The four Tarot suites are all corner stones of certain parts of Hermetic (and most Western) ritual magic. Pentacles, cups, coins and blades are all used in rituals and rites, and each has a lot of mystical significance and meaning behind them. They're also the basis behind modern playing cards (Swords = Spades, Coins = Diamonds, Cups = Hearts, Pentacles = Clubs). The simplest way to build off of the Tarot as far as foci/tools would be using some sort of blade (ceremonial dagger or sword, or the like), a ritual cup/chalice, one or more coins or gemstones of significance, and chalk or other implements for drawing pentacles. (Alternately, if you're into the sort of modernist Chaos magic influenced Hermeticism that House Thig was big on, you could swap those out for their modern equivalents like a gun and credit cards.) Language/chanting/writing is also a big Hermetic focus. Especially of you can learn the True Names of certain spirits or other entities tied to certain cards.<br /> <br /> The Awakened also have their own associations for parts of the Tarot. Back in the day, there was even a <i>Mage Tarot Deck</i> made, which the included booklet discussing the suites' associations with both the four Avatar Essences and the four factions of the Ascension War (Traditions, Technocracy, Marauders, Nephandi), and the Major Arcana's associations with various WoD elements. (It also had suggestions for using it as a method of character creation and as a ST tool in various ways.) You can get a reproduction of it from DriveThruRPG's <a href=\"https://www.drivethrucards.com/product/223145/Mage-The-Ascension-Tarot\" target=\"_blank\">DriveThruCards section</a>.<br /> (I've long wished I could get the Sons of Ether-as-The Chariot and the Euthantos-as-Wheel of Fortune images blown up to poster size.)<br /> <br /> And thou it was made for Mage: The Awakening, the <i>Keys to the Supernal Tarot</i> book has a lot of interesting ideas to mine.<br /> <br /> And if you've never read Alan Moore's Promethea, it delves into a lot of classic Western mysticism, including an entire issue devoted to explaining the Major Arcana of the Tarot as the magicians journey from the ignorance of the Fool to the enlightenment of The World/Universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct me if I'm wrong, No One of Consequence, but I was under the impression that Coins and Pentacles were the same/interchangeable - i.e. take up the same &quot;place&quot; in various versions of Tarot - and that the fourth suit was <i>Staves/Wands</i>.<br /> <br /> Which, of course, have occult applications, both generally and to the hypothetical Tarot-based Focus, that need no introduction.<br /> <br /> <br /> (As an aside, the Coins-Pentacles association may have its roots in &quot;pentacles&quot; being specifically arcane designs etched or molded onto metal disks, that are worn as pendents. There are, like, dozens of Solomonic Seals, the descriptions of many of them specifically calling for putting them on pendents made of specific metals.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 09-10-2020, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T21:03:08-07:00","id":1412958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1411362-advice-about-a-tarot-based-mage?p=1412910#post1412910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong, No One of Consequence, but I was under the impression that Coins and Pentacles were the same/interchangeable - i.e. take up the same &quot;place&quot; in various versions of Tarot - and that the fourth suit was <i>Staves/Wands</i>.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>(doh!) Yes, you are correct.<br /> <br /> And obviously, the focus/tool associated with Staves/Wands is the traditional wizard's wand, staff, or rod. (Which is the pretty blatant masculine phallic symbol meant to counterpart the feminine womb of the cup/bowl/cauldron. Discussion about how the Hermetics are typically associated with wands and the Verbena with cauldrons is entirely optional.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 09-11-2020, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T22:42:31-07:00","id":1413914,"title":"","content":"Just passing by to tell you the idea was a BIG SUCCESS. <br /> <br /> I used another cartomancer mage (NPC) to tell her about the importance of allegories and elements represented in the Cards. And of course, the importance of dominating the &quot;lesser secrets&quot; too. &quot;Becoming the arcana&quot; would be a future lesson. That Cartomancer, by the way, will be one of the main antagonists. I needed an excuse to bring her character closer to him (so his future betrayal could be emotially tough for her) and this one was perfect. She's now not trusting her official mentor and trusting the cartomancer more...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T08:14:12-07:00","id":1413971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1411362-advice-about-a-tarot-based-mage?p=1413914#post1413914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just passing by to tell you the idea was a BIG SUCCESS.<br /> <br /> I used another cartomancer mage (NPC) to tell her about the importance of allegories and elements represented in the Cards. And of course, the importance of dominating the &quot;lesser secrets&quot; too. &quot;Becoming the arcana&quot; would be a future lesson. That Cartomancer, by the way, will be one of the main antagonists. I needed an excuse to bring her character closer to him (so his future betrayal could be emotially tough for her) and this one was perfect. She's now not trusting her official mentor and trusting the cartomancer more...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Given how he's leading her astray, I wonder if the Cartomancer has come to embody The Devil more than any other Major Arcana.<br /> <br /> Then again, a cursory glance at Wikipedia says that The Devil tends to represent a half-knowledge of things, and a fixation on earthly matters as opposed to spiritual ones. The Cartomancer seems to know some of what he's doing, and is instructing the PC in more abstract matters.<br /> <br /> On the <i>other</i> other hand, he is leading the PC on. I don't know what his deal is or what he plans. It would just be appropriate if he turned out to be overselling his knowledge and obfuscating his ulterior motives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T08:19:07-07:00","id":1413972,"title":"","content":"I did a bit more digging on Wikipedia, and The Hermit was also looking pretty appealing for your Cartomancer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A.E. Waite's Pictoral Key to the Tarot</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">9.THE HERMIT.--Prudence, circumspection; also and especially treason, dissimulation, roguery, corruption. Reversed: Concealment, disguise, policy fear, unreasoned caution.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 09-16-2020, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T12:56:10-07:00","id":1414020,"title":"","content":"This really feels like you could take any (or all) of the ideas presented here and let the player use those as a springboard to character development (a way to evolve their understanding of magic and how they use it and their dependence on foci by considering the relationship between the symbols and their meaning to the mage as a person.) Coming to some realization about that would free them towards the expanded options and greater flexibility suggested in so many ideas (either by broadening the symbols that can attach to a meaning, or her willingness to adapt that symbolism as circumstances permit.) IIRC Mage even has different 'grades' of foci which could also be reflected here.<br /> <br /> You could even get to a point where the mage can simply 'draw' their own tarot foci (even if they're low grade ones) using some sort of paper and pen (maybe they need to develop their artistic skill and do research before they achieve this though) So given a little preparation and improvisation they're never without 'cards' - and it reminds me a bit of the 'magical prayer paper strip' thing you sometimes see in anime to boot. Although I admit when I saw this thread the first thing I thought of was the Hermetic equivalent of Gambit from X-men using magically charged playing cards to cast spells lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T15:41:48-07:00","id":1414277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1411362-advice-about-a-tarot-based-mage?p=1414020#post1414020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Although I admit when I saw this thread the first thing I thought of was the Hermetic equivalent of Gambit from X-men using magically charged playing cards to cast spells lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, she's actually a big fan of Card Captor Sakura. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T15:56:50-07:00","id":1414281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1411362-advice-about-a-tarot-based-mage?p=1413971#post1413971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the <i>other</i> other hand, he is leading the PC on. I don't know what his deal is or what he plans. It would just be appropriate if he turned out to be overselling his knowledge and obfuscating his ulterior motives.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1948 a riot destroyed a big part of my city. Someone killed a beloved politician and people wanted to burn the place to the ground in response. The alleged killer (think of him as our Lee Harvey Oswald) was known for his interest in the Occult, and for seeing a mysterious german fortune teller the days before the assasination (all of that is real life history). The mob lynched him so we never knew who sent him (for that matter, we actually never knew if he was the real killer), and nobody made any research on the fortune teller either (we only know his name and a short statement about his relation with the suspect).<br /> <br /> My chronicle is set in the 1940s. I decided to make that real life fortune teller a hermetic widderslainte (I ditched the idea of a proper barabbi cause I didnt picture him serving a dark force or whatever) who foresees when big tragic events will happen in the world, devoting himself to make them happen. He sees himself as a trigger of that. He became part of the local chantry by selling himself as someone running from from WW2 (to have access to Quintessence), and is, in secret, just pulling the strings to make the riot happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}